# scripts/

Operational scripts for ${PROJECT_NAME}.

## What lives here

- One-off CLI utilities (migrations runner, data fixers, kb-sync, etc.).
- Shell scripts that wrap repetitive `npm` / `docker` flows.
- File-size lint check (`check-file-size.sh`) — invoked by `npm run lint:size`.

## What does NOT live here

- Application HTTP / business logic. That belongs under `${SRC_DIR}/api/`.
- Database models. Those live under `${SRC_DIR}/models/`.
- Framework-agnostic helpers. Those go in `${SRC_DIR}/lib/`.

## Naming

- `*.ts` for TypeScript-based scripts (run via `tsx` in dev or compiled in CI).
- `*.sh` for plain bash helpers.

## Linked files

- [`run-migrations.ts`](run-migrations.ts) — runs `migrations/postgres/*.sql` in order.
- [`check-file-size.sh`](check-file-size.sh) — warns when a `.ts` file exceeds 500 lines.
- [`tsconfig.scripts.json`](tsconfig.scripts.json) — extends the root tsconfig for script compilation.

